he  simple concept behind vh1's dating naked  contestants disrobe down to their  birthday suits and went on dates such as  sipping cocktails by the pool or  engaging in some light mud wrestling  romantic right although the participants  needed to bare it all during filming  they were apparently promised that their  naughty bits would be blurred out when  the show air unfortunately whoever was  in charge of the blurring  made a major error during the July 31st  2014 broadcast then 28 year old model  Jesse News wits was wrestling with her  date on the beach when viewers caught a  brief unblurred glimpse of her private  parts Miz which quickly became the  target of ridicule across social media  and filed an ultimately unsuccessful 10  million dollar lawsuit against vh1 owner  Viacom along with two of the show's  production companies eventually the  Parents Television Council who were  staunchly against the show managed to  wrestle 90% of dating make its corporate  advertisers away from the series the  show was canceled shortly after its  third season in 2017 with poor ratings  cited as one of several reasons for the  decision  good grief if you thought the world of  funeral homes was an untapped treasure  trove of reality gold well there might  be a reason for that  in 2014 lifetime was set to produce good  grief a reality series that centered  around the Johnson family mortuary in  Fort Worth Texas but the series wound up  six feet under before it ever got off  the ground on July 15th 2014 the  landlord paid his tenants a visit and  discovered eight rotting bodies hidden  beneath the funeral home when reporters  and paparazzi showed up owner Dondre  johnson initially told the spectators  that's great advertising because in a  few days from now we'll be on a reality  show so I want all this media ultimately  Johnson was found guilty of theft for  stealing money from customers and  neglecting the bodies of their loved  ones in sentenced to two years in prison  and a fine of $10,000 unsurprisingly the  network pulled the plug  [Music]
 

